{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.MirrorAsymmetrySign","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MirrorAsymmetrySign","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.c1Closed_mirror_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.c1Closed_mirror_ne","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MirrorAsymmetrySign.lean#L151-L160","doc":"The same statement as a strict monotonicity in the proton excess: at fixed\n`A ≥ 3`, moving a neutron to a proton strictly increases `c₁`. (Corollary of\n`c1Closed_step` and the bracket's sign; recorded because it is the form the\nisospin reading uses.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.c1Closed_mirror_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.c1Closed_mirror_pos","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MirrorAsymmetrySign.lean#L137-L149","doc":"**The prediction.** For `A ≥ 3` and more protons than neutrons, the derived\nleading-order coefficient is strictly larger for the proton-rich member: the trace\nchannel says it binds MORE. Measured against AME 2020 this is the wrong sign in\nall 230 mirror pairs — see the module docstring and the probe. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.mirrorBracket_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.mirrorBracket_pos","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MirrorAsymmetrySign.lean#L117-L135","doc":"**The general sign.** For every `A ≥ 3` the bracket is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.mirrorBracket_neg_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.mirrorBracket_neg_two","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MirrorAsymmetrySign.lean#L110-L115","doc":"**The A = 2 boundary case: the bracket is negative.** `5·2 = 10 < 13`. Mirror\npairs at `A = 2` are the diproton and dineutron, neither of which is bound, so\nnothing is measured here — but the sign genuinely flips and the general claim\nbelow must exclude it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.mirrorBracket_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.mirrorBracket_eq","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MirrorAsymmetrySign.lean#L100-L108","doc":"`4^{−A}·(5·2^{A−1} − 13)` is the bracket: the sign is that of `5·2^{A−1} − 13`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.c1Closed_mirror_diff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.c1Closed_mirror_diff","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MirrorAsymmetrySign.lean#L79-L94","doc":"**[★]** The mirror difference of the derived `c₁`, exactly. Stated for\n`1 ≤ Z` and `1 ≤ N` so that both truncated interface counts are honest\nsubtractions (`I_pp = Z−1`, `I_nn = N−1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.mirrorBracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.mirrorBracket","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MirrorAsymmetrySign.lean#L57-L77","doc":"The mirror bracket `5·2^{−A−1} − 13·4^{−A}`, which carries the entire\n`(Z,N)`-dependence of the leading-order mirror asymmetry.\n\n**This file survived the 2026-09-06 `c1Closed` repair unchanged, and that is not\nluck.** Owner ruling `qou-hu1f` reordered the atom word and `c₁`'s per-nucleon\ncoefficients moved from `(21, 16)` to `(3, −2)` — every one of the six recorded\nvalues changed, by up to `163×`. Nothing here moved, because the mirror\ndifference cancels everything except the coefficient *gap*:\n\n    c₁(Z,N) − c₁(N,Z) = (Z − N)·[ (P − Q)·(2^(−A−1) − 2^(−2A)) − 8·2^(−2A) ]\n\nso `mirrorBracket` depends on `P − Q` alone, and `P − Q = (S_p − S_n)/2` is `5`\nunder **both** orderings — `(42 − 32)/2` and `(6 − (−4))/2`. The `13` below is\n`(P − Q) + 8`, likewise fixed by it. That equality of gaps is **measured on the\ntwo words, not derived**: nothing shown here forces a third ordering to give `5`\nas well, so treat this file's invariance as verified-for-these-two rather than\nstructural, and re-check `P − Q` before quoting it for any new word. Contrast\n`PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.chain_over_atom_He4_of_letters`, whose `24/7` **is**\nstructural — there the letter weights cancel identically, for every `(a, b)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}